    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διόπτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>looker through,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ Ζεῦ διόπτα</span>! says Dicaeopolis
			in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				435
			</span></i>, holding up a ragged garment to the light. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			= foreg. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
